quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  20,114,"So exalted is Allah, the Real Sovereign, the Ultimate Truth. And be not in haste with the Qur’an before its revelation to you is completed. And say: ‘My Lord! Increase me in knowledge.’"
  20,115,"And indeed, We made a pact with Adam earlier, but he forgot. And We did not find any intention (of disobedience) in him."
  20,116,"When We said to the angels: ‘Prostrate yourselves before Adam.’ They prostrated, except Iblis. He refused."
  20,117,"Then We said: ‘O Adam! This is indeed an enemy of yours and your wife’s. Therefore, do not let him expel you both from Paradise; in that case, you may face hardship."
  20,118,"Indeed, you shall neither be hungry in it nor naked."
  20,119,"And indeed, you shall neither be thirsty in it nor suffer from the sun.’"
  20,120,Then Satan whispered to him and said: ‘O Adam! Shall I show you the Tree of Eternity and a kingdom that will never diminish?’
  20,121,"Then they both ate from it, and their private parts became exposed to them. So they began to stitch the leaves of Paradise over themselves. And (in this way) Adam failed to observe his Lord’s command. So, he missed the mark (and thus could not achieve eternal life).*"
  20,122,"Then his Lord chose him (for His proximity), turned to him (with mercy) and guided (him to repentance)."
  20,123,"He said: ‘Get down from here, all together, being enemies of one another! And if guidance should come to you from Me, then whoever follows My guidance will not go astray, nor will he be miserable."
  20,124,"And whoever turns away from My remembrance, there shall be indeed a depressing life for him. And We shall raise him blind on the Day of Resurrection.’"
  20,125,"He will say: ‘My Lord! Why have You raised me blind, though I used to see (before)?’"
